/**
 * Picture prompts for every mystery scene card (cards/my-NN-*) and Real Ending
 * (mysteries/<case>/<ending>), keyed by the art asset the game looks up. Each
 * describes only what is visible, in plain prose that reads the same on all
 * four Ecotone art styles. Ported from conductor weird-humboldt
 * art/ART-STANDARD-ROUND-2.yaml and rewritten where a line was figurative.
 */
export const MYSTERY_ART_PROMPTS: Record<string, string> = {
  'cards/my-01-g1':
    'A wide view of a gravel turnout on a mountain road at night, fog rolling down the hill all at once. About twenty people in matching blank orange beanies sit in folding chairs or stand by fence posts strapped with trail cameras, all raising glowing phones toward the road. A young man points at a parked station wagon with a perfectly round dent in its door, the paint scuffed in a ring; a bill and a small jar of honey sit under the wiper. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the edge, from behind.',
  'cards/my-01-g2':
    'A wide view of an old shearing shed on a ridge top at night, stars overhead and a white sea of fog below with dark hilltops poking through it. Inside, under a work light, sit strange homemade racing carts: a church pew on go-kart wheels, a clawfoot bathtub with flame decals, a coffin-shaped cart. Elderly racers in leathers and cardigans stand around them. A shaggy white ram in a red bandana stands in the middle eating a granola bar. A blank road-crew paddle hangs by the door. A figure in a weathered rain jacket watches from the doorway.',
  'cards/my-01-g3':
    'A wide view of a blind curve on a narrow mountain road at night. A group of people in blank orange beanies has strung a cargo net across the road between two fence posts, and a young man in front grins in the flashlight glow. Fog is pouring over the shoulder, swallowing the road beyond the bend, while tiny lights glimmer on the starlit ridge above. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands on the shoulder off to one side, seen from behind, holding a bundle of unlit road flares.',
  'cards/my-01-cold':
    'A wide view of a gravel turnout on a mountain road on a clear morning after the fog has burned off. A tangled cargo net lies in a heap at the roadside beside folded camp chairs and empty coffee cups. Thin, narrow tire tracks cross the damp gravel next to a line of hoofprints that run into the oak and fir trees and simply stop. Dew shines on the grass and a faint mist lingers in the hollows. Far up the ridge sits a small shed with its door closed.',
  'cards/my-01-reveal':
    'A wide view of a gravel turnout at night as the fog thins and every flashlight swings to one spot. There sits a long, low cart built from a hospital gurney chassis, hay bales lashed to the nose and a padded bumper ringed in safety orange. Its driver wears leathers and a welding helmet with two enormous curling horns. A shaggy white ram in a crooked red bandana pants beside it. Behind, eight more homemade carts have stopped, elderly drivers lifting their goggles. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands in the road, from behind.',
  'cards/my-01-b-unmasked':
    'A medium view of a gravel turnout at night in thinning fog. An old man of seventy-one with a silver flattop standing straight up and a wind-burned face holds a horned welding helmet under one arm, his other hand patting the gurney cart beside him. A blank road-crew paddle leans against the cart. An elderly woman in a blank orange beanie gasps in recognition, and behind him a row of old racers in leathers and cardigans nod. A shaggy white ram in a red bandana stands nearby. A figure in a weathered rain jacket is at the edge.',
  'cards/my-01-b-rematch':
    'A wide view from the top of a ridge at night, the stars so bright they crowd the sky and a white sea of fog below. Homemade gravity carts line up at the head of a road that curves away into the cloud. A figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind, sits in a church pew on wheels; beside it a driver in a horned welding helmet waits in a gurney cart. A shaggy white ram stands out front, and an old man in a bathtub cart lets a red bandana fall.',
  'mysteries/kneeland-ram/first-down':
    'A wide view of a mountain road at night as a slow procession of homemade carts rolls down through thin fog. A shaggy white ram in a red bandana trots at the very front, ahead of a gurney cart driven by someone in a horned helmet, then a bathtub cart and a coffin-shaped cart. At the very back, a figure in a weathered rain jacket rides a church pew on wheels, seen from behind. People on foot in inside-out orange beanies hold flashlights at every bend, making warm pools of light.',
  'mysteries/kneeland-ram/ram-stays-wild':
    'A wide view of a mountain road at night, thick with fog. A car has pulled onto the gravel shoulder with its hazard lights blinking, its headlight beams cutting into the mist. Through the beams runs a shaggy white ram in a red bandana, and close behind it a low, shadowy cart slips into the fog, its driver only a faint horned silhouette. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands beside the open car door, seen from behind, letting it pass.',
  'mysteries/kneeland-ram/headfirst':
    'A wide view down a fog-filled mountain road at night. A shaggy white ram in a red bandana runs ahead, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket runs after it, seen from behind. The road beneath them changes as it recedes, from cracked asphalt to oiled gravel to two ruts in the grass. On each stretch a flagger stands on the center line in the fog, one in a hard hat, one in a canvas coat, one in a wool cap, each turning a blank paddle and waving the ram through.',
  'cards/my-02-g1':
    'A wide view inside a cool cheese-aging cave dug into the foot of a hill. Wooden shelves hold rows of golden cheese wheels under a single warm bulb, but one low shelf is completely bare, and fresh scrape marks run through the damp, gritty floor to an open back door. Through the door, dairy cows graze only on the hillside while the flat green fields below sit empty. A young woman in an apron, gold-green paint on one wrist, holds out a tasting board. A figure in a weathered rain jacket is seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-02-g2':
    'A wide view of flat, deep green river-bottom pasture along a slough under an overcast sky. A grid of orange-flagged survey stakes runs across the field, and a tidy pile of pulled stakes sits by the wooden gate. Twenty dairy cows stand in a line at the fence, all watching. A man holds his surveying rod raised high in one fist and waves a folder, while his partner calmly eats a sandwich beside him. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands near the gate, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-02-g3':
    'A wide view of a hilltop at night under a full moon. An old wooden hay barn stands with its door ajar and a faint light inside. Below, thick white tule fog lies flat across the low fields, silver in the moonlight. On the slope, a dairy herd is rising to its feet all at once. A figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind, stands at the barn with a key in hand, a big wheel of cheese under one arm and a paper bag of bread.',
  'cards/my-02-cold':
    'A wide view of flat, green river-bottom fields on a grey afternoon. A new wire fence now surrounds the low field, and rows of orange-flagged survey stakes stand firm in the grass. By the road, a small open-house tent shelters a folding table of refreshments and strings of plain bunting, with a few people holding paper cups. Up on the green hillside beyond, the dairy herd stands in a line beside a white barn, standing perfectly still.',
  'cards/my-02-reveal':
    'A wide view inside an old hay barn at night. On a hay bale sits a person in a homemade felt calf costume, slightly deflated, its glow paint smudged across the felt nose and giving off a faint green light. New wooden shelves around the walls hold wrapped cheese wheels with blank labels. In the wide-open doors, forty real dairy cows press in shoulder to shoulder, breath steaming in the moonlight, every head turned toward the calf. A figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind, holds up a phone.',
  'cards/my-02-b-rosie':
    'A medium view inside an old hay barn at night, lit by a lantern. A young woman of twenty sits on a hay bale in a felt calf costume, the felt head in her lap, glow paint smeared on her eyebrows and a volleyball kneepad sliding down one shin. Through the creaking door comes her grandmother, eighty and five feet tall, in a long flannel nightgown and gumboots, carrying a steaming kettle with a stern look. Cows crowd the moonlit doorway behind her. A figure in a weathered rain jacket sits at the edge.',
  'cards/my-02-b-second-calf':
    'A wide view of the edge of a low, marshy field at night, fog lying close to the ground. A small calf stands in the wet grass glowing a warm milky gold from inside its body, its light spilling across the reeds and the slough water as it looks back, waiting. Up the slope the herd stands lowing. A young woman in a felt calf costume holds the felt head and stares, while an old woman in a nightgown and gumboots sets down a kettle. A figure in a weathered rain jacket is seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/stubborn-herd/herd-knows':
    'A wide view of an open house in a flat green field on an overcast afternoon. Strings of plain bunting hang over a folding table of refreshments, and along the fence forty dairy cows stand in a silent line, every head turned to the low fields. A young woman in a felt calf suit walks forward with the head under her arm, and an old woman holds up a big hand-drawn field map. A surveyor nods while his partner quietly pulls up her own orange stakes. A figure in a weathered rain jacket holds up an open folder, seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/stubborn-herd/sold-conditions':
    'A wide view of a dry coastal marsh in late summer, dairy cows grazing among the tidal channels below a green hill topped with a white creamery barn. The low ground holds open marsh, fence posts, cordgrass and a pair of egrets. In the foreground, on a weathered picnic table, sits a wheel of cheese freshly cut open beside a knife, a folded felt calf costume in tissue paper and an old hand-drawn field map. A figure in a weathered rain jacket rests their hands on the table, seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/stubborn-herd/golden-calf':
    'A wide view of a dark pasture at night as river water rises through the grass with a long, slow ripple. Up the slope, a young woman of eighteen with a dish towel tied over her hair carries a lantern and leads forty dairy cows uphill in a line. At the very front walks a small calf glowing a warm milky gold from inside its body. Half-drowned fence posts stand in the flood. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands knee-deep in the water, seen from behind, watching them pass.',
  'cards/my-03-g1':
    'A wide view of a small fishing harbor on a foggy morning, a long wooden pier stretching toward a rocky headland. A wet spaniel stands stubbornly on the deck of a moored fishing boat while its owner pleads from the dock. At the end of the pier an older woman sets down her coffee as the man beside her looks stricken, and everyone else glances at the sky. By a bait shop window with a plain hand-painted board, a woman in a fleece vest stands beside an old radio, waving. A figure in a weathered rain jacket is seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-03-g2':
    'A medium view of a fishing pier on a drizzly morning. A middle-aged man in a bright yellow rain slicker, a scar through one eyebrow, grins and winks as he carries off a paper-wrapped bundle of sardines from the fish counter. Beside him, a woman in a fleece vest holds up her phone, which shows a photo of the very same face scowling in a dark bar. The other fishermen keep their eyes on their nets. Behind them a trail climbs a forested headland into the fog. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the edge.',
  'cards/my-03-g3':
    'A wide view of the back of a fishing harbor at dusk, sea spray rising over the breakwater and fog rolling in. Behind the bait shop stands a weathered wooden net loft hung with nets, a thin wire antenna running up its side, and a warm light glowing under its door. A woman in a fleece vest holds a portable radio and gives a sideways look. Stacked crab pots line the wet gravel. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands in the alley before the door, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-03-cold':
    'A wide view inside a small bait and tackle shop at six in the morning. On the counter sits an old portable radio, its dial set to an empty station, and a woman in a fleece vest leans close with a coffee mug, listening hard. Fishing lures hang on pegboard behind her. Through the fogged window, out on the misty pier, a man in a yellow slicker is cheerfully buying sardines. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the edge of the room, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-03-reveal':
    'A medium view inside a cramped net loft turned into a closet-sized radio station. A homemade transmitter built from a car stereo and a toaster hums on the bench, its meter needle still moving beside a microphone. On two stools sit two identical middle-aged men with the same eyebrow scar, one in a yellow rain slicker, one in a bar apron, both looking caught. Behind them a wall is covered in pinned paper slips. In the doorway, a woman in a fleece vest stares at the antenna. A figure in a weathered rain jacket is seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-03-b-two-men':
    'A medium view inside a cluttered net loft radio station at night. Two identical middle-aged brothers, one in a yellow rain slicker and one in a bar apron, sit on stools by a homemade transmitter, both going red. In the open doorway stands an older woman in a knit cap, and behind her an older man holds out a round cake tin. A woman in a fleece vest holds the door, looking thoroughly betrayed. Harbor lights glow in the fog outside. A figure in a weathered rain jacket sits at the edge.',
  'cards/my-03-b-your-voice':
    'A close view of a homemade transmitter inside a net loft at night, built from a car stereo and a toaster, its meter needle swinging. An old loudspeaker grille glows faintly with a haze of static around it. A figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind, leans toward the microphone to answer it. In the background two identical brothers, one in a yellow slicker and one in a bar apron, have gone pale, and a woman in a fleece vest stands by the door. Warm bulb light meets teal shadow.',
  'mysteries/second-voice/two-of-a-kind':
    'A wide view of a harbor pier on a late afternoon, one long table running its whole length. In the middle sits a single cake with two sets of lit candles, and two identical middle-aged brothers lean over it side by side, one blowing out his candles while the other cries happily. Fishermen in rubber boots crowd the benches arguing about who knew first, and an older woman at the end has the table laughing. String lights hang over the moored boats. A figure in a weathered rain jacket sits at the table, seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/second-voice/one-life':
    'A medium view of a small kitchen table by a window at dawn, the foggy harbor and its pier visible beyond the glass. An old radio glows on the windowsill beside a steaming mug of coffee. Two hands hold open a folded handmade paper birthday greeting with drawings in two different inks. A weathered rain jacket hangs on the back of the chair. Far out on the misty pier a tiny yellow slicker moves among the boats.',
  'mysteries/second-voice/talk-to-yourself':
    'A medium view inside a net loft radio station at dawn. A figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind, sits on a stool leaning into the microphone of a homemade transmitter whose dial glows softly. Through the small window, the fog is lifting off the harbor and first light turns the water pink and amber. Two coffee mugs sit on the bench, and in the corner two identical brothers, one in a yellow slicker and one in a bar apron, doze against the wall of pinned paper slips.',
  'cards/my-04-g1':
    'A medium view of a small living room in a low house by the bay at dawn. An old woman sits in her recliner with arms folded beside a steel crab pot holding nine angry Dungeness crabs, dripping onto her braided rug. A hand-painted buoy is tied to the pot, and a folded stick of gum lies on the windowsill. Through the window, a neighbor in a yellow rain jacket hoses out a skiff on a trailer in the drizzle and waves. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands off to one side.',
  'cards/my-04-g2':
    'A wide view of a boatyard on a quiet slough at dusk, old skiffs with grass growing in them and a tug sinking into its cradle. At the end of a crooked wooden dock, half hidden in cordgrass, floats a thirty-eight-foot wooden crab boat. Woodsmoke rises from her stovepipe, red geraniums bloom in a coffee can on the wheelhouse roof, and a blank red tag is zip-tied to her rail. A lamp glows in the wheelhouse. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands by a chalk-marked piling, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-04-g3':
    'A wide view of a low street on the edge of the bay before dawn. Every porch light is on, and neighbors sit on their steps in coats over their pajamas, an old woman wrapped in a blanket, a man in a yellow rain jacket. Beyond the houses, a rocky point of riprap disappears into mist so thick the channel lights look underwater. Out on the dark water a single boat light is coming in. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands on the shore holding a lantern, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-04-cold':
    'A wide view from a small front porch beside the bay on an overcast morning. On the boards sits an empty crab pot, scrubbed clean, with a brass crab gauge tied to its handle, and the porch light is still on. Across the slough, in a boatyard, a crew in hard hats is breaking apart an old wooden boat, its split planks piled beside a tow truck. Gulls circle over the grey mudflats in the fog.',
  'cards/my-04-reveal':
    'A wide view of a little wooden dock on the bay at first light, an old wooden crab boat tied at its end with its engine still ticking. Thirty neighbors in rubber boots crowd the planks around a figure in yellow oilskins whose hood has just come back: an old man with a white beard trimmed square and bright, tired eyes. With big, scarred hands he measures a crab against a brass gauge. An old woman presses a hand to her mouth. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands among them, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-04-b-aboard':
    "A medium view inside a cramped eighty-square-foot wooden wheelhouse packed with one old man's belongings. A tiny woodstove glows beside a bunk covered by a quilt patched from old yellow oilskins. On the chart table lie a pair of folded reading glasses and a calendar pinned open to an old month. On a rack by the stove hang two lopsided hand-painted snail mugs, one chipped and full of coffee, one clean. An old man with a square white beard and a wool sweater gestures around the room with an open hand. A figure in a weathered rain jacket is at the edge.",
  'cards/my-04-b-porch-council':
    'A wide view of a little wooden dock at dawn crowded with thirty neighbors in rubber boots and borrowed coats. In the middle, a steel crab pot serves as a coffee table loaded with thermoses and paper cups. An old woman speaks to the crowd while a young man types notes on his phone. A man in a yellow rain jacket holds out a box of donuts to an old crabber with a square white beard. Woodsmoke from the boat at the end of the dock drifts up the street. A figure in a weathered rain jacket sits among them.',
  'mysteries/crab-pot-ghost/home-port':
    'A wide view of a sunny marina dock on the opening day of crab season. The old wooden crab boat sits in her own tidy slip, with new curtains in the wheelhouse, a freshly welded rail and geraniums on her roof. Potluck tables run along the dock, and neighbors line up with paper plates. An old man with a square white beard serves steaming crab, a brass gauge at his elbow, and hands the first plate to a figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/crab-pot-ghost/last-haul':
    'A close view of a modest apartment front door on a grey king-tide morning. From the door handle hangs a mesh bait bag holding a polished brass crab gauge and a folded, blank paper note. Wet footprints lead across the doormat. Behind, the king tide has pooled at the edge of the street, reflecting the overcast sky, and a window box of red geraniums glows faintly under a porch light in the drizzle.',
  'mysteries/crab-pot-ghost/moored-in-1970':
    'A wide view of a rocky point of riprap at four in the morning, the bay flat and dark under thick mist. Out on the empty water two silver wakes run side by side, heading in toward shore. On the hood of a parked car an old marine scanner glows softly. Behind, on an empty lot where front steps once stood, a full crab pot waits. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands on the rocks, seen from behind, watching the wakes.',
  'cards/my-05-g1':
    'A wide view backstage at an old vaudeville theater on a wet night, ropes and sandbags overhead and sawdust on the boards. The stage door is propped open with a fishnet-wrapped brick. A dozen cast members in fully clothed cabaret costumes and lab coats argue at once around cold pizza boxes, while a young man in a glam costume and heels stands with his arms crossed. A trail of gold sequins glints across the floor toward the dark. Through a doorway, a woman in a silk headscarf paces with a phone.',
  'cards/my-05-g2':
    'A wide view from an old projection booth at night. An elderly projectionist with steady hands threads a mystery reel, and the beam crosses an empty auditorium through drifting dust. On the far screen, a shadow audience from 1981 fills red velvet seats in shoulder pads and satin jackets, a performer in a golden lion mask dances onstage, and a small girl in a homemade gold cape mouths along. In the third row, one empty aisle seat catches falling rice. A figure in a weathered rain jacket watches from behind.',
  'cards/my-05-g3':
    'A wide view of an old vaudeville theater packed for its last midnight show, every seat and aisle full of costumed fans as the house lights dim. High in the roped-off balcony, a silver-haired woman with perfect eyeliner sits alone with a paper bag of lemon drops. At the back wall a woman in a silk headscarf stands arms folded beside a man in a blazer clicking a tally counter. In the wings a nervous young performer stretches his calves. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands in the side aisle, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-05-cold':
    'A wide view of an old theater auditorium the morning after it closed. A distant crew in hard hats unbolts the red velvet seats and stacks them in the aisles, leaving bare floor bolts behind, while dusty daylight pours in from an open door. The stage is empty under work lights. In the foreground, on one remaining seat, lies an open theater program with blank pages and a single gold sequin taped inside. Through the lobby doors the old marquee hangs dark.',
  'cards/my-05-reveal':
    'A wide view of a packed old theater the moment the music ends. At center stage, in a single spotlight, a human performer in a glittering golden lion mask and sequined mane headdress takes a deep bow, chest heaving. Around them the costumed cast stands frozen, and in the wings a young man in a glam costume stares open-mouthed. Up in the balcony a silver-haired woman has set down her lemon drops. The house lights rise amber, the old way. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands in the front row, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-05-b-unmasked':
    'A wide view of a packed old theater with the mask just off. At center stage stands a middle-aged woman with long black hair pinned flat, perfect eyeliner and her chin up, holding a golden lion mask at her side, folded papers tucked at the waist of her sequined costume. Four hundred faces gasp. High in the balcony, a silver-haired older woman has risen to her feet and points down at her. At the back wall a man stares at his tally counter. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the stage edge.',
  'cards/my-05-b-encore':
    'A medium view of the wings of an old theater after an a cappella encore. A performer in a sequined costume kneels with head bowed, and a young man in a glam stage costume lifts the golden lion mask off with both hands, revealing a woman with long black hair pinned flat and perfect eyeliner. Beyond the curtain the whole audience is on its feet, a silver-haired woman standing in the balcony. High in the booth window, an old projector blinks a small red light. A figure in a weathered rain jacket watches from behind.',
  'mysteries/midnight-mane/long-live':
    'A wide view of an old theater with the house lights up and rice flying through the air. On stage, a woman with long black hair in a sequined costume tears a document in half, a golden lion mask at her feet. A silver-haired older woman comes down to dance the turn with her, then a young man in a glam costume, and soon the whole house is doing it badly together. An old man passes around a blank clipboard. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands in the aisle, seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/midnight-mane/one-more':
    'A medium view of a small, cluttered apartment on a rainy evening. A pair of old red velvet theater seats with worn gold trim, still bolted together, is crammed between a bookshelf and a radiator, far too big for the room. A single gold sequin rests on one cushion. A framed painting of a red stage curtain hangs above them. A figure in a weathered rain jacket sits in one seat with a mug of tea, seen from behind, the other seat empty beside them.',
  'mysteries/midnight-mane/reel-1981':
    'A wide view of an empty theater at night where an old projector throws a flickering film onto the screen. The film shows this same room in 1981: red velvet seats, gold walls, a crowd in shoulder pads and satin jackets. In its third row, one empty aisle seat catches falling rice in perfect time, beside a small girl in a homemade gold cape. On the projected stage, a golden lion dances with a long black braid swinging under the mane. A figure in a weathered rain jacket watches from the seats.',
  'cards/my-06-g1':
    'A wide view of a gravel pullout where a side canyon meets a wide green river, a dark forested ridge rising above. A hatchback is parked crooked on the gravel, a red ribbon tied in a neat tight bow on its side mirror. Two students huddle under one blanket in the back seat. An anxious young woman holds out a blank paper flyer with torn pushpin holes. River fog drifts below in the fading light. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the edge, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-06-g2':
    'A wide view of a steep deer trail at night entering a grove of enormous old redwoods, trunks twenty feet across with deeply furrowed bark. Every tree wears a red ribbon tied at exactly the same height, and some carry a lower blue ribbon beside a spray-painted number. Higher up the slope, lanterns move from trunk to trunk, carried by distant robed silhouettes. Mist drifts among the ferns. A figure in a weathered rain jacket climbs the trail with a flashlight, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-06-g3':
    "A wide view of an ancient redwood grove under a huge orange harvest moon that turns the ridge the color of old brass. Robed figures in plain brown hoods circle the widest tree, holding a long red ribbon between them by lantern light. One small figure stands apart, clutching a padded case to her chest. Behind a fallen log, four students crouch with a ring light. Down the slope, a pickup's headlights grind up a logging road. A figure in a weathered rain jacket crouches in the ferns, seen from behind.",
  'cards/my-06-cold':
    'A medium view inside a small-town laundromat on an overcast day. A cork bulletin board is crowded with blank flyers, and in its center someone has pinned one neat white paper slip beside a short red ribbon. Washing machines line the wall under flat fluorescent light. Through the big front window, across the river valley, a forested ridge now shows a fresh bare scar of logging road and stumps where tall trees used to stand.',
  'cards/my-06-reveal':
    'A wide view at the base of a colossal redwood at night, lanterns glowing in the mist. Eight retired women in plain brown robes have turned and lowered their hoods. The tallest has close-cropped white hair and a pencil behind each ear; beside her a botanist clutches a padded case, and another holds a thick binder and a diameter tape. A long red ribbon circles the giant trunk. Nearby a student slowly lowers a ring light. A figure in a weathered rain jacket faces them, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-06-b-the-count':
    'A wide view of an old-growth redwood grove in the grey before dawn. A figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind, holds a diameter tape level around a giant trunk and reads it. Beside them an older woman in a brown robe writes in a thick binder, while a botanist checks another tree and a thermos of tea passes down the line. Lanterns are dimming in the mist. Across a ravine stands one last tree, and above them all looms the eldest redwood.',
  'cards/my-06-b-the-cruiser':
    'A medium view of a dirt logging road at night below a redwood grove. A tired man in his thirties in a high-visibility vest leans against an open pickup, its headlights on, and holds out a tablet with a cracked, glowing blank screen. A can of blue marking paint hangs from his other hand, and a thermos cup of tea sits on the hood. Behind him, trunks bear blue spray-painted numbers and red ribbons, and the lights of a small town glow in the valley below. A figure in a weathered rain jacket is seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/virgin-sacrifice/every-tree-counted':
    'A wide view of an old-growth redwood grove on the first clear morning after winter, sunbeams slanting through the mist. Around the eldest, colossal trunk, retired women in brown robes and college students in matching robes hold a diameter tape together while one reads the number aloud. A white-haired woman with pencils behind her ears watches the number hold, and another writes it in a binder. A figure in a weathered rain jacket wears a brown robe over it, a pencil sewn into the sleeve, seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/virgin-sacrifice/one-tree-saved':
    'A wide view of a logged ridge at dusk under a rising harvest moon. Where a forest stood there are now stumps, slash piles and open sky, but in the middle a single colossal redwood still stands within a small buffer of neighbor trees, a seabird nest on one broad limb. Older women in brown robes climb the bare slope toward her with lanterns. A figure in a weathered rain jacket holds the end of a diameter tape, seen from behind, the river valley spread out below.',
  'mysteries/virgin-sacrifice/ring-for-next-year':
    'A close view of a wooden worktable in the back room of a small-town library. Under a magnifying loupe lies a pencil-thin core of redwood, and its growth rings keep going past the center, each smaller than the last, down to the width of a hair and beyond. A glass specimen tube with a blank paper label waits beside it, along with pencils and a coiled diameter tape. Small wooden catalog drawers and shelves of binders fill the room. A figure in a weathered rain jacket leans over the loupe, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-07-g1':
    'A wide view of a quiet side street in a Victorian dairy town, houses painted butterscotch and teal with gingerbread trim. Between two front porches runs an ancient wooden fence that leans in both directions at once. On one porch an old man in a cardigan holds a weathered fence board across his chest; on the other an old woman grips a ceramic garden gnome. Blank cream paper squares are pinned to both front doors. A young woman waits at the corner, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket stands off to one side. Soft fog and muted daylight fill the street.',
  'cards/my-07-g2':
    'A wide night view of a terraced hillside cemetery of white marble headstones and old cypress trees, the lights of a small town glowing far below. Near the top, a table stands on a flat granite marker, set with a gavel, an open ledger and polished brass scales that catch the moon. Behind it sits a magistrate in a black robe and a long curled wig yellowed at the edges, face lost in shadow. Two veiled ushers in mourning black hold lanterns at either end, perfectly still. Two empty chairs face the bench, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket stands before them, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-07-g3':
    'A wide afternoon view of a Victorian main street, storefronts in butterscotch and teal, the whole town out gossiping in little knots. Blank flyers are pinned to every post, and in the open doorway of a feed-and-tack store men lean over a blank chalkboard holding out folded bills. At a shop window an old woman admires a brand-new hat. Behind the rooftops rises a steep green hill dotted with white headstones. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the edge of the street, looking up at the hill. Soft fog drifts through amber light.',
  'cards/my-07-cold':
    "A quiet morning porch on a Victorian house with teal trim. On a small wooden table sits an olallieberry pie in its tin, cut into two perfect halves. Dew beads on the railing and an empty rocking chair. Past the steps, the old fence between this house and the next still leans in both directions at once, and a ceramic garden gnome sits on the neighbor's porch step. Pale fog fills the empty street.",
  'cards/my-07-reveal':
    'A wide lantern-lit night scene at the top of a hillside cemetery. At a table on a granite marker, a bald, kindly old man in a black robe blinks in surprise, his long curled wig dangling from the gavel and from the hand of a figure in a weathered rain jacket seen from behind. Beside the bench, two ushers have their mourning veils lifted: a blushing young man and a young woman holding his hand. Families sit in folding chairs on either side, an old man in his good jacket and an old woman in a new hat, while half the town peeks from behind headstones.',
  'cards/my-07-b-open-court':
    'A lantern-lit hearing among white headstones on a hill at night. An old woman in a new hat stands and reads aloud from a yellowed handwritten recipe, while a bald old man in a black robe listens at the table beside the brass scales. Across from her, an old man in his good jacket sits very still, eyes wet. Families in folding chairs lean in. Far below, the dark town shows only two porch lights burning side by side. A figure in a weathered rain jacket watches from the edge.',
  'cards/my-07-b-the-weighing':
    "A close view of antique brass scales on a granite table at night, their two pans held perfectly level. In one pan rests an old man's weathered hand, in the other an old woman's. In the polished brass beneath each hand, two faint pictures shimmer on the metal: a holiday dinner table with one empty chair, and a long pale hospital hallway. Behind the scales, a bald old man in a black robe has gone pale, staring. Lantern light glints on the brass, and blurred headstones and cypress trees fill the dark beyond.",
  'mysteries/midnight-magistrate/court-adjourned':
    'A wide night view of a Victorian side street lit by lanterns and porch lights. Two families in their good clothes are taking apart an old wooden fence with crowbars, an old man and an old woman each wrenching loose a board while younger relatives hold up flashlights. Neighbors watch from every porch. An upright piano waits on a dolly in the street, and a gavel hangs from the last remaining fence post. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the edge, holding a paper plate of pie.',
  'mysteries/midnight-magistrate/fair-split':
    'A symmetrical wide view of two Victorian houses facing each other across a fence that now runs perfectly straight, marked by fresh survey stakes. In each front window hangs a frame holding one half of an old blue prize ribbon, cut cleanly down the middle, each half turned toward the other house. Each porch has its own small white wedding arch and its own row of chairs, exactly alike. A pair of sewing scissors rests on one porch rail. Flat gray overcast fog light lies over both houses.',
  'mysteries/midnight-magistrate/older-docket':
    'A wide night view from a country road up to a hillside cemetery, a car parked on the shoulder with its headlights on. Among the white headstones and cypress trees, faint lanterns glow between the graves. A translucent judge in a yellowed curled wig sits behind a bench with brass scales, hearing two families of pale, glowing figures in clothes from the 1890s, bowler hats, bonnets and long skirts. Mist drifts between them. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands beside the car, looking up the hill.',
  'cards/my-08-g1':
    'A wide view inside a rustic ridge-top tavern with wood paneling and a glowing woodstove. On the bar, laid out on a folded white towel, are three bottle caps, a gold wedding ring and a brass key in a perfectly straight line. Behind the bar an elderly Japanese American woman wipes her hands beside a coffee pot and a jar of pickled eggs. Four students in muddy rain shells lean in around the towel. A flickering half-lit red neon tube glows in the rain-streaked window, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket sits at the end of the bar, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-08-g2':
    'A wide view of a lonely homestead clearing high on a forested ridge. An old cabin sits with its porch slumped to one knee, a blue plastic bin on the railing. In the middle of the clearing stands a split redwood stump, ringed by fresh, shallow holes and little heaps of dirt. Crows line the cabin roof and a broken fence, watching. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the edge of the clearing holding a stack of postcards. Overcast light and mist on the ridge.',
  'cards/my-08-g3':
    'A wide dusk view of a mountain clearing where dozens of crows have settled silently around a split redwood stump. From the dark tree line steps a towering costumed figure, seven feet of shaggy black plastic feathers with a long pickaxe-shaped beak mask, clearly a person on stilts. Down the rutted dirt road, a pair of headlights is coming fast, beams full of dust. The masked figure turns its head between the lights and a figure in a weathered rain jacket standing near the cabin. The sky fades purple and amber above the firs.',
  'cards/my-08-cold':
    "A close view of a worn wooden bar top in a ridge tavern. An old woman's hand sets down a steaming mug of coffee beside a bar towel where three bottle caps, a gold ring and a brass key still lie in a perfectly straight row. Behind them, a woodstove glows and a rain-streaked window looks out at a dusky ridge, where small black crows are gathering in the distance. Warm amber lamplight falls across the bar.",
  'cards/my-08-reveal':
    'At dusk in a mountain clearing, a sunburned woman in her forties sits on a split redwood stump wearing a homemade costume of black contractor bags cut into feathers. She has taken off her beak mask and holds it in her lap; her legs still end in drywall stilts, and a paint can full of bottle caps on a broom handle leans beside her. A ring of school-bus keys hangs from a lanyard at her neck. Dozens of crows sit quietly around her boots. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands nearby, and below, a foggy river valley fades into the evening.',
  'cards/my-08-b-care-home':
    'A quiet care home common room late at night, lit by a single warm lamp. An elderly man in a cardigan buttoned wrong sits at a table covered in blank white postcards, carefully drawing a simple stump, an arrow and a setting sun in pencil. A Pacific Islander aide in scrubs and slippers stands at his shoulder, smiling. A tired sunburned woman in her forties watches from across the table, her hands folded. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands by the side door, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-08-b-wrong-side':
    'At sunset in a ridge-top clearing, a fresh hole has been dug on the west side of a split redwood stump, a shovel stuck in the dirt beside it. In the hole sits a big rusted coffee can, its old tape peeled back to show a small roll of bills and a bundle of envelopes in a plastic bread bag. A sunburned woman kneels at the edge, and all around the hole a silent ring of crows stands waiting. One crow hops forward to drop a brass key into the can. A figure in a weathered rain jacket watches nearby, long shadows stretching east.',
  'mysteries/crow-court/crows-remember':
    'A wide view of a ridge-top clearing at dusk. An elderly man in a borrowed wheelchair lifts both arms high, and crows sweep in over the ridge to land on him, on his wrists, his shoulders and the brim of his cap. A Pacific Islander aide stands behind the chair, grinning, and a sunburned woman with a headlamp holds a rusted coffee can full of letters at his side. Behind them stand the split redwood stump and the old cabin. A figure in a weathered rain jacket watches from the edge as the purple sky fills with wings.',
  'mysteries/crow-court/let-it-stay-buried':
    'Looking out through the open door of an old cabin at dusk. Just inside the doorway, a homemade cloak of black plastic feathers and a beak mask hang on a nail. Outside, in the clearing, crows have gathered around a split redwood stump, heads bowed over the smooth undisturbed ground. At the edge of the clearing a woman leans against her pickup truck, watching them. Firs stand dark against an amber and violet sky, and low fog drifts across the ridge.',
  'mysteries/crow-court/blue-bin':
    'A wide view of a ridge-top clearing at dusk. Dozens of crows stand on the ground and the stump and the cabin rail, every one of them turned toward a figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind, who holds a metal scoop over a blue plastic bin of peanuts. On the cabin porch rail lies a brass gate key. A dead oak stands on the ridge behind, and the valley below is full of fog. The amber light is fading, and the birds are perfectly silent.',
  'cards/my-09-g1':
    'A wide view of a clifftop trailhead parking lot above a long black sand beach, the mountains rising straight up behind and spray drifting off the surf. A blank wooden warning board stands at the trail, and wedged neatly behind it is an arrow: a straight driftwood shaft, a filed slate point and three white feather fletches. A young man with a scraggly beard holds out the back of his hand, where simple map lines are drawn in marker. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands beside him, seen from behind, looking north into the spray.',
  'cards/my-09-g2':
    'A wide view of a river mouth where a clear river spreads over a gravel bar into the sea, golden coastal hills rising on both sides. An old sheep rancher in a battered hat leans on a fence post with an arrow stuck in it, his ewes milling at a wooden gate. Down on the gravel bar, a line of large hoofprints comes up out of the water, crosses the stones and climbs straight up a steep bluff. Behind the rancher, an old barn stands with its door open on a bolt of white sailcloth. A figure in a weathered rain jacket listens at the edge.',
  'cards/my-09-g3':
    'A wide night view of a black sand beach at the bottom of a minus tide, the wide wet sand shining beneath steep, dark mountains. Far down the beach, two men in matching safety vests pull arrows out of driftwood logs and drop them into garbage bags by headlamp. Out of the fog to the north gallops a huge gray horse with a cloaked rider low on its back, the two merged into one long silhouette. A young bearded man and a figure in a weathered rain jacket, both with headlamps, stand in the foreground as the surf begins to creep back in.',
  'cards/my-09-cold':
    'A close view of a blank wooden trailhead board above a black sand beach, with a tidy empty gap behind it where an arrow used to be wedged, now stuffed with a wad of gum. Beyond, the tide is high and the waves have swallowed the black sand right up to the driftwood logs. The mountains disappear into gray fog and light rain. The parking lot behind it stands empty in the drizzle.',
  'cards/my-09-reveal':
    'A wide night view of a small camp high in a mountain meadow: a fire ring, a spring, a tarp, and four crates of damp, swollen paperbacks. Beside the fire, an enormous gray horse calmly grazes. Next to it stands its rider, a gray-haired person in their sixties in an oilskin coat, glasses with one lens taped, a quiver of driftwood arrows on their back and a ring of fletching thread on a carabiner. They hold out a single arrow toward a figure in a weathered rain jacket, seen from behind. Stars hang over the dark ridge.',
  'cards/my-09-b-what-it-cost':
    'Close by a campfire high in the mountains at night. A gray-haired former professor in an oilskin coat, glasses with one lens taped, feeds a stick into the flames and looks steadily across the fire. A quiver of driftwood arrows leans against a crate of swollen paperbacks, and a big gray horse rests in the dark beyond the tarp. Sparks rise into the deep blue night. A figure in a weathered rain jacket sits across the fire, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-09-b-arrows-i-didnt-make':
    "A close view of a tarp spread by a mountain campfire at night, laid with twelve driftwood arrows fletched in white feathers. Each arrow has turned on the tarp to point in a different direction out into the dark. One arrow points straight at the gray-haired archer in an oilskin coat who kneels at the tarp's edge. Firelight flickers on the slate points, and a gray horse stands as a silhouette behind. A figure in a weathered rain jacket kneels off to one side.",
  'mysteries/wandering-arrows/coffee-for-ten':
    'A wide view of a mountain meadow camp at first light, mist lifting off the ridge. Eight search and rescue volunteers in reflective vests crowd around the fire, holding enamel cups. A gray-haired archer in an oilskin coat grinds coffee in a hand mill with a furious expression, while every arrow is laid out on a tarp for the team. An older woman in a reflective vest takes notes on a blank pad beside a duffel bag stuffed with driftwood arrows. A gray horse grazes nearby, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket holds a worn paperback at the edge.',
  'mysteries/wandering-arrows/rider-moves-on':
    'A morning view of the trailhead above a long black sand beach. The wooden trailhead board has a fresh coat of plain paint, and wedged neatly behind it is one last driftwood arrow with white fletching, pointing up the trail toward the parking lot. Far up the beach, a tiny gray horse with a rider and full saddlebags heads north into the sea fog beneath the steep mountains. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands by the board, seen from behind, watching them go.',
  'mysteries/wandering-arrows/arrow-at-her':
    "At the gray end of the night, a figure in a weathered rain jacket steps out of the trees holding a driftwood arrow and finds the same mountain camp from the other side. By the dying fire, a gray-haired archer in an oilskin coat sits hunched with knees drawn up and hood pulled up, and lifts a tired face toward the newcomer. Down at the figure's side, the back of one hand shows a faint drawn route running east. Mist fills the ridges, and a gray horse waits by the crates of books.",
  'cards/my-10-g1':
    'A wide view of an old pier on pilings the color of burnt toast, running out into a foggy bay. Behind it, a dead pulp mill looms with one tall smokestack raised into the fog. Wet cloven hoofprints, each pair followed by a long smooth drag mark, climb out of the water across the planks and stop at the base of the stack, beside an abandoned bolt cutter and a coil of stripped copper wire. A bundle of fresh eelgrass is tied to a piling at the end. A tow truck driver leans on her bumper with a donut box and a crowbar, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket studies the prints.',
  'cards/my-10-g2':
    'A wide view of a street of tidy, freshly painted company cottages with sand dunes rising behind them. On one front step, an elderly Latina woman re-canes a porch chair, head bent over her work. Two doors down, a cottage has a lawn mowed in perfect stripes and a lit garage window. Through the glass you can see a sewing machine, a laptop with a blank glowing screen, and something long and green draped over the workbench, half covered by a tarp. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands on the sidewalk, peering in. Soft fog, late afternoon light.',
  'cards/my-10-g3':
    "A wide midnight view of an old mill pier on a foggy bay. By a rusted ladder the water has gone flat and glassy, and out of it rises a strange shape: curling horns, a shaggy beard, broad shoulders, and a long scaled tail that thumps the planks. Down the pier, a scrap crew with their headlights off freezes beside a cutting torch, while a tow truck's amber beacons sweep the gravel lot beyond. At the base of the towering smokestack, a brass whistle sits on a dead pipe. A figure in a weathered rain jacket crouches off to one side.",
  'cards/my-10-cold':
    'A gray morning at the gate of an old mill pier. A shiny new padlock hangs on the chain-link gate beside a blank county notice. Beyond, the weathered pier runs out into a foggy bay, and the tall smokestack is just a smokestack again. In the foreground, through the windshield of a parked tow truck, a little plastic goat and a plastic fish are zip-tied together on the dashboard. Gulls drift over the eelgrass in the shallows.',
  'cards/my-10-reveal':
    'Forty rungs up a dead mill smokestack, on a small railed platform high above the fog, sits a person in a magnificent handmade sea-goat costume, breathing hard: a hand-sewn wetsuit, a beard of dyed rope, horns of steam-bent wood, and a long fishtail of hundreds of green neoprene scales hanging over the edge. A trail camera blinks red on the rail. Far below, a dive tank is strapped to the base of the stack, its hose running to a brass whistle, and tow truck beacons sweep an empty gravel lot. A figure in a weathered rain jacket has climbed up beside it.',
  'cards/my-10-b-foreman':
    'From the top of a dead mill smokestack at night, a woman in her thirties sits with a homemade sea-goat hood pushed back, eelgrass tangled in her ponytail, a bagged form clipped to her neoprene suit. She has gone silent, staring down. Far out past the pier and the eelgrass plots, a head the size of a rowboat has risen from the black water: horns each the size of a car wheel well, a beard of living kelp, one green eye turned up at the stack. A figure in a weathered rain jacket grips the rail beside her. Fog drifts in the moonlight.',
  'cards/my-10-b-shift-change':
    'Looking down from the top of a mill smokestack at true midnight. The bay lies perfectly flat and glassy, and something enormous has surfaced at the foot of the stack: horns the size of wheel wells, a beard of living kelp, and a scaled tail that runs back into the dark water farther than the pier is long. It has set one hoof on the bottom rung of the ladder and waits there. On the platform, a woman in a homemade neoprene sea-goat costume grips the rail with both hands, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket leans out beside her.',
  'mysteries/sea-goat/the-climb':
    'A wide night view of an old mill pier crowded with elderly retirees in faded mill work jackets, taking turns on the chain of a big brass whistle while a plume of air blasts out over the black bay. An elderly Latina woman stands at the front, calling the shifts. Beside her, a woman in her thirties talks on a phone, and a tow truck idles with its beacons turning. Across the water, porch lights in the far town are coming on one by one. A figure in a weathered rain jacket steps up to take the chain.',
  'mysteries/sea-goat/whistle-stops':
    'A quiet autumn afternoon on the porch of a painted company cottage. A big brass whistle rests on the boards beside a freshly caned porch chair, silent. Past the dunes, the old mill pier now has a new fence along it, and the shallows beneath are thick and green with eelgrass. On the step, a cardboard box holds a folded costume with wooden horns sticking out the top. The smokestack stands far off in soft fog, and the low sun turns everything amber.',
  'mysteries/sea-goat/half-new':
    'Seen from the wet deck of a crab boat coming in late across the bay at night, crab pots stacked by the rail. Up on top of the old mill smokestack sit two horned silhouettes against the fog, one in sleek neoprene and one rough and crusted with barnacles. In the dark channel beside the boat, a second wake keeps pace, far too long for any vessel. A figure in a weathered rain jacket leans on the rail, looking up. The moon glows dimly behind the clouds.',
  'cards/my-11-g1':
    'A wide dawn view of a potholed country road where every house is on a well. On a porch sits an old gallon glass dairy jug with a finger loop, full of crystal-clear water that bends the porch light, a strip of blank tape on its side. A Black woman in her sixties, a retired bus driver, stands beside it with her arms folded. Across the road a man in a bathrobe holds his own jug up to the rising sun, and more jugs sit on porches down the line. A figure in a weathered rain jacket holds a jug off to one side. Morning mist over the pastures.',
  'cards/my-11-g2':
    'A wide midnight view of a gravel bar on a rushing river beneath cottonwoods. A dozen people sit on coolers with binoculars, passing a thermos. Above a deep pool hovers a ring of cold white light, and from it a thin line drops into the water, hangs, and reels back up. An old man in a camp chair watches unimpressed. Far off, a pickup sits at the bridge turnout with its lights off, and high among the stars something smaller hangs perfectly still. A figure in a weathered rain jacket sits at the edge, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-11-g3':
    "A wide view of a meadow on a back road at early morning, a clawfoot bathtub full of rainwater standing in the field. Beyond it rises a ruined geodesic dome, its triangles grown through with blackberry. Under tarps inside, hundreds of glass water jugs stand on tall shelves in neat rows. Beside the dome stands a hand-dug well with a rotted crank and a dark, dry mouth, and a workbench holds a hand-cranked well sounder. Over the ridge, a ring of white light is coming in low, straight for the well. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands in the dome's doorway.",
  'cards/my-11-cold':
    "A close view of a kitchen windowsill at dawn where an old glass dairy jug of clear water sits unopened, a strip of blank tape on its side, catching the light and throwing small rainbows. Through the window, the rural road runs past neighbors' porches; one lawn has a blank white board staked in it, and a well-service truck is parked in a driveway. Potted herbs line the sill. Soft morning mist hangs over the road.",
  'cards/my-11-reveal':
    'First light over a meadow by a ruined geodesic dome. On the grass lies the downed UFO: a rented survey drone wrapped in a ring of party lights, a speaker zip-tied to its belly and a sonar sounder on a line. Its pilot sits on the cattle guard in a camouflage hunting poncho, night-vision goggles pushed up on his forehead, holding out a small blank white slip of paper. Up the road comes a woman in a waxed canvas hat and muddy boots, pushing a hand truck stacked with empty glass jugs, and she stops short. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands between them.',
  'cards/my-11-b-the-buyer':
    'A misty morning at a cattle guard on a back road. A man in a camouflage hunting poncho, night-vision goggles on his forehead, gestures casually toward a dry hand-dug well, a folded list in his other hand. Across from him a woman in a waxed canvas hat and muddy boots has sat down heavily on her hand truck of glass jugs, shoulders slumped. A drone wrapped in party lights lies on the grass, and the ruined geodesic dome stands behind them. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands between them, seen from behind.',
  'cards/my-11-b-the-well':
    'Beside an old hand-dug well with a rotted wooden crank, a woman in her sixties in a waxed canvas hat rests one hand on a glass water jug and looks down into the dark, dry throat of the well. A coil of old rope lies at her feet. Behind her the ruined geodesic dome is overgrown with blackberry, and a clawfoot bathtub sits in the field. Faint and translucent beside her, a fully clothed child in a 1970s shirt lowers a bucket into the same well. A figure in a weathered rain jacket listens at the edge. Soft golden mist.',
  'mysteries/water-bearer/water-for-everyone':
    'A wide summer view of a golden meadow beside a ruined geodesic dome. A woman in a waxed canvas hat tips a glass jug of river water down the mouth of an old dry well, while a dozen gray-haired former ranchers stand around her in a loose circle, some laughing, most crying. On a barn roof down the valley, new rain tanks gleam. Overhead a secondhand drone flies a slow survey in plain white light. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands at the back of the circle, seen from behind.',
  'mysteries/water-bearer/jugs-stop':
    'Inside a ruined geodesic dome, blackberry vines push through the triangular frame and shafts of late-summer light fall across long rows of bare wooden shelves. The tarps have been pulled back and the workbench cleared. On one shelf, alone in all that emptiness, stands a single glass dairy jug, full to the shoulder with clear water, a strip of blank tape on its side catching the light. Dust drifts in the warm air; outside, the meadow grass has gone dry and gold.',
  'mysteries/water-bearer/contact':
    "A wide night view of a deep pool on a river, cottonwoods dark along the gravel bar. Just above the black water hovers a glass jug with a finger loop, glowing from within, the water inside it swirling upward. Its glow lays a long reflection across the pool. At the water's edge a woman in a waxed canvas hat stands very still, a painted mark on the rock beside her, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket watches from the bar. Stars and river mist.",
  'cards/my-12-g1':
    'A bright, windy late afternoon on a wide beach. A young fire spinner, her spinning chains worn as a belt, cradles a green felt busking hat in both cupped hands. Its felt is gray with salt, a ring of tiny brass bells circles the brim, and it is full of frosted sea glass in greens and ambers with one bright cobalt piece. A folded blank sheet of paper sticks out of her pocket. Up on the bluff, an old van sits in the parking lot. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands beside her, seen from behind, and the surf rolls in teal and white.',
  'cards/my-12-g2':
    "A wide dusk view of a river sliding across a broad sand bar into the ocean, sea stacks to the north. On a near rock, a man in a long wig and a shiny costume tail waves at a dozen tourists unloading from a tour van on the pullout. Farther out, on a rock at the river's edge, a woman in a long-sleeved top and a homemade fabric tail sits singing, and from the bluff the two rocks line up into one creature with two tails. Every seal on the bar has turned toward her. A retired man hands binoculars to a figure in a weathered rain jacket, and smoke rises from the driftwood under the bluff.",
  'cards/my-12-g3':
    'A wide sunset view of a beach of sea stacks and mirror-wet sand, the sky blazing orange. Out on a far rock at the river mouth, someone has set a tiny stage: a ring of sea glass on the stone and one battered juggling torch, unlit. In the foreground, two jugglers, a hula hooper, an accordion player and a crepe vendor with a cart have crept out from behind the driftwood logs. Up on the pullout a tour van unloads tourists, while a man in a shiny mermaid tail wades toward the near rock with a speaker in a dry bag. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands in the middle of it all.',
  'cards/my-12-cold':
    'A close view of a green felt busking hat set on a wooden bench in a small town plaza, a ring of tiny brass bells around its salt-grayed brim. It is heaped with frosted sea glass in greens and ambers, and right on top sits a single heart-shaped cobalt piece. Behind it the plaza lawn and passersby are soft and blurred, a juggler practicing far off. Soft overcast afternoon light falls across the bench.',
  'cards/my-12-reveal':
    'At deep twilight on the rocks of a river mouth, a red-faced man in his forties sits soaked in the shallows in a shiny costume tail, a headset mic askew, his long wig floating away on the tide beside a dead speaker. On the far rock, a woman in a long-sleeved top and a homemade mermaid tail sewn from old faded vinyl, weighted with fishing sinkers at the fin, holds a real burning torch and stares at him. A figure in a weathered rain jacket has crossed the sand bar to the foot of her rock, and a young fire spinner stands frozen in the water behind.',
  'cards/my-12-b-coral':
    'On high, dry sand above a river mouth at dusk, a woman in a long-sleeved top and a homemade mermaid tail made from old faded vinyl sits against a driftwood log, stage paint smudged, talking quietly. A young fire spinner with chains for a belt sits close and holds her hand. Behind them the tide has started to cover the sand bar, and a few seals bob in the gray water near the sea stacks. A figure in a weathered rain jacket sits with them, seen from behind. A guttering torch stuck in the sand gives a little warm light.',
  'cards/my-12-b-two-currents':
    "At dusk, river and sea meet over a sand bar in a long seam of foam, and the singer's reflection splits along it. In the river-side water shimmers a crowded town plaza where a woman juggles fire for families; in the sea-side water, a harbor town kitchen where the same woman fries fish and sings. On the rock above, the woman in a homemade vinyl mermaid tail and long-sleeved top watches both. A young fire spinner and a figure in a weathered rain jacket stand on the sand nearby. Purple and gold dusk light.",
  'mysteries/two-tailed-mermaid/both-tails':
    "A wide night view of a beach below a bluff, lit by a driftwood bonfire. A woman in a homemade vinyl mermaid tail and long-sleeved top juggles flaming torches in slow arcs, sea glass glinting at her feet. Half the town's street performers and a few tourists sit on driftwood logs in rapt silence, and out on the sand bar a row of seals watches too. High on the pullout, a man in a wet sequined tail looks down alone. A young fire spinner waits with a green felt hat in her hands, and a figure in a weathered rain jacket sits on the nearest log.",
  'mysteries/two-tailed-mermaid/let-her-swim':
    'A soft spring evening at a river mouth. Under the bluff, where a driftwood camp once stood, the sand lies smooth and swept clean. The far rock is bare. Out on the sand bar, fourteen seals have hauled out, and a retired man in a fishing hat counts them with binoculars, pencil poised over his waterproof notebook. Wildflowers dot the bluff and the sky is pink with mist. A figure in a weathered rain jacket stands beside him, looking out at the empty rock.',
  'mysteries/two-tailed-mermaid/other-current':
    'A close view on a lonely rock at a river mouth at dusk, where a ring of sea glass lies on the stone. A hand in a weathered rain jacket sleeve holds one piece up to the sunset, a color somewhere between teal and gold. Inside it, very small, are two pictures of the same woman waving: one on a busy town plaza, one in a harbor town up the coast. Behind the glass, the river and the sea meet in a long seam of foam beneath the sea stacks.',
}
